- What metrics would you expose to observe fairness and SLA adherence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-hop, CKNE-aware backpressure and fairness across thousands of tenants with SLA-based tuning.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health as a control signal for fan-out
- Per-tenant token bucket and dynamic scaling
- SLA-tier influences on limits and queuing
- Edge backpressure signaling and aggregation
- Payload schemas and end-to-end test plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimit(health, queueLen, sla) {
  const base = 1000;
  if (health > 0.8 && queueLen < sla.maxQueue * 0.7) return Math.min(base * 5, sla.maxCap);
  if (health < 0.4 || queueLen > sla.maxQueue * 0.9) return Math.max(base * 0.2, sla.minCap);
  return base;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world BI workloads multiplex dozens to thousands of tenants; CKNE-driven concurrency and memory control is critical for SLOs and fair sharing.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource mapping: concurrency, memory budget, spill/IO throttling
- Per-tenant quotas and dynamic reallocation cadence
- Fairness guarantees and explicit preemption rules
- Telemetry hooks and feedback for regret-free adjustment

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocate(tenants){
  // normalize CKNE 0-1 to weight, compute quotas
  const total = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ t.alloc = t.ckne/total; });
  return tenants;
}
```

